$DATUM (R)-N-[1-(3-Methoxyphenyl)ethyl] 3-(2-chlorophenyl)propanamide, 42R. To a
solution of 3-(2-chlorophenyl) propionic acid 41 (48 mg, 0.257 mmol) at
room temperature, under argon atmosphere, in dry CH2Cl2(2 mL),
dicyclocarbodiimide (DCC) (58 mg, 0.282 mmol) anddimethylaminopyridine
(DMAP) (3.16 mg, 0.10 equiv.) were added. After stirring for 1 h at rt,
40R (38.8 mg, 0.257 mmol) was added and then stirring during 1h. The
reaction mixture was filtered through a pad of Celite and the solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure.The obtained crude was purified by
flash chromatography (EtOAc:hexane, 3:1). The desired compound 42R (78,41
mg, 96%) as a white solid. mp 96°C; [α]D 20 = +47 (c1.0 in CHCl3); 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.31-7.20 (m, 5H), 6.82-6.80 (m, 3H), 5.51 (d, 1H, J=
7.0 Hz), 5.09 (c, 1H, J= 7.0 Hz), 3.81 (s, 3H), 2.99 (t, 2H, J= 7.5 Hz),
2.50 (t, 2H, J= 7.5 Hz), 1.42 (d, 3H, J= 6.9 Hz) ppm; 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 171.0, 159.8, 144.7, 140.8, 129.7, 128.5, 128.4, 126.2, 118.4,
112.5, 112.3, 55.2, 48.7, 38.6, 31.7, 21.6 ppm; HRMS: calcd for C18H21NO2
[M+H-Cl]+: 283.1572; found: 283.1570.
