$DATUM 2-Amino-4-bromo-N-(((2S*,5R*)-5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-methyl)benzamide
(rac-8b). DIPEA (1.15 mL, 6.94 mmol) and HATU (1.32 g, 3.47 mmol) was
added to the suspension of 2-amino-4-bromobenzoic acid (5) (0.5 g, 2.31
mmol) in dry DCM (20 mL), and the mixture was stirred at rt for 15 min.
Then 5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methanamine (rac -7b) (0.36 mL, 3.47
mmol) was added, and the mixture was stirred at rt for 2 h. The solvent
was then removed in vacuum, and the remaining residue was purified by
column chromatography (1/1 = EtOAc/PE), Compound rac -8b (0.664 g, 96%
yield) as colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.75-1.93 (m, 2H),
2.08-2.16 (m, 1H), 2.30-2.38 (m, 1H), 3.40-3.47 (m, 1H), 3.78-3.84 (m,
1H), 4.23 (qd, J = 3.5 Hz, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 4.91 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 5.61
(brs, 2H), 6.40 (brs, 1H), 6.68 (dd, J = 2.0 Hz, 8.2 Hz, 1H), 6.81 (d, J
= 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.04 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.25-7.36 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3): δ 28.9, 33.9, 43.5, 78.4, 81.4, 114.5, 119.46, 119.52,
125.9, 126.5, 127.6, 128.5, 142.3, 149.9, 168.7. MS (ESI) m/z (relative
intensity): 375.3 (100%), 376.3 (34.7%), 377.3 (99.9%), 378.3 (33.8%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
