$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2-Amino-4-bromo-N-(((2S*,5R*)-5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-methyl)benzamide
(rac-8b). DIPEA (1.15 mL, 6.94 mmol) and HATU (1.32 g, 3.47 mmol) was
added to the suspension of 2-amino-4-bromobenzoic acid (5) (0.5 g, 2.31
mmol) in dry DCM (20 mL), and the mixture was stirred at rt for 15 min.
Then 5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methanamine (rac -7b) (0.36 mL, 3.47
mmol) was added, and the mixture was stirred at rt for 2 h. The solvent
was then removed in vacuum, and the remaining residue was purified by
column chromatography (1/1 = EtOAc/PE),
2-Amino-4-bromo-N-((tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methyl)benzamide (rac-8a).
Prepared in analogy to compound rac-8b. Yield 0.67 g (96%), colorless
oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ 1.52-1.60 (m, 1H), 1.74-1.93 (m, 3H),
3.18-3.29 (m, 2H), 3.59-3.64 (m, 1H), 3.73-3.79 (m, 1H), 3.94 (pent, J =
6.3 Hz, 1H), 6.61 (brs, 2H), 6.64 (dd, J = 2.0 Hz, 8.6 Hz, 1H), 6.90 (d,
J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.41 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 8.32 (t, J = 5.9 Hz, 1H). 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 25.8, 28.6, 43.2, 68.1, 77.6, 114.6, 119.35,
119.44, 126.3, 128.5, 149.8, 168.6. MS (ESI) m/z (relative intensity):
298.9 (100%), 299.9 (19.8%), 300.9 (92.2%), 301.9 (18.9%).
